1
00:00:01,084 --> 00:00:04,004
[BEA] <i>Billy said I was a thief.</i>

2
00:00:04,671 --> 00:00:07,340
<i>But she's the original thief herself!</i>

3
00:00:07,424 --> 00:00:09,676
[BILLY] <i>Do you know what caused the fire?</i>

4
00:00:09,759 --> 00:00:11,469
[CLERK] <i>No one knows, miss.</i>

5
00:00:11,553 --> 00:00:15,015
<i>All I heard was that Mariela survived.</i>

6
00:00:15,098 --> 00:00:16,558
<i>And so did her youngest daughter.</i>

7
00:00:16,641 --> 00:00:19,269
<i>But her eldest daughter died.</i>

8
00:00:19,352 --> 00:00:22,105
[BILLY] <i>But the father wasn't with them?</i>

9
00:00:22,188 --> 00:00:25,650
[CLERK] <i>The rumor is that</i>
<i>Mariela's husband left her.</i>

10
00:00:26,276 --> 00:00:27,318
<i>Ma.</i>

11
00:00:28,236 --> 00:00:29,696
<i>I spoke with the lawyer.</i>

12
00:00:30,196 --> 00:00:33,658
<i>She said it's possible</i>
<i>you'll be moved to a hospital.</i>

13
00:00:33,742 --> 00:00:36,077
<i>You won't rot here anymore.</i>

14
00:00:36,161 --> 00:00:37,579
<i>You can get out.</i>

15
00:00:38,163 --> 00:00:39,414
<i>Which hospital?</i>

16
00:00:39,497 --> 00:00:40,999
<i>The…</i>

17
00:00:43,626 --> 00:00:44,586
<i>ward.</i>

18
00:00:44,669 --> 00:00:47,338
<i>- Crazy. She's going to a psych ward.</i>
- [MARIELA] <i>Wait, the psych ward?</i>

19
00:00:47,422 --> 00:00:49,090
<i>- What am I, crazy?</i>
- [LAUGHS]<i> She admitted it.</i>

20
00:00:49,174 --> 00:00:51,050
<i>You want to be away from me, right?</i>

21
00:00:51,134 --> 00:00:53,261
- [WOMAN]<i> It came from her.</i>
<i>- Ma, no. You're not crazy.</i>

22
00:00:54,429 --> 00:00:58,099
<i>Ma, just think about it.</i>
<i>You'll be better off there.</i>

23
00:00:58,183 --> 00:00:59,601
<i>You'll be taken care of.</i>

24
00:01:00,268 --> 00:01:02,103
<i>Turns out she really is crazy.</i>

25
00:01:02,187 --> 00:01:04,022
- [WOMEN CACKLING]
- <i>She belongs there.</i>

26
00:01:04,105 --> 00:01:05,857
<i>- Ma. Hey, Ma!</i>
<i>- Hey!</i>

27
00:01:05,940 --> 00:01:07,484
<i>- Let go of me! Ouch!</i>
<i>- Stop it, Ma!</i>

28
00:01:07,567 --> 00:01:09,319
- [WOMAN] <i>Stay out of this!</i>
- [BEA] <i>What the hell?!</i>

29
00:01:09,402 --> 00:01:11,279
<i>- Stop it!</i>
<i>- Ma! Ma!</i>

30
00:01:11,362 --> 00:01:13,239
- [GRUNTS SOFTLY]
- <i>Ma!</i>

31
00:01:13,865 --> 00:01:14,783
<i>- Come on.</i>
<i>- Cheers.</i>

32
00:01:14,866 --> 00:01:16,159
<i>- Cheers!</i>
<i>- Cheers!</i>

33
00:01:16,242 --> 00:01:17,285
<i>Happy second anniversary!</i>

34
00:01:17,368 --> 00:01:18,703
<i>- Cheers, everyone!</i>
<i>- Cheers, guys!</i>

35
00:01:18,787 --> 00:01:19,788
<i>- Oh, yes.</i>
<i>- Cheers!</i>

36
00:01:19,871 --> 00:01:22,749
[BLAIRE] <i>Good thing those menaces are</i>
<i>behind bars now, chief.</i>

37
00:01:22,832 --> 00:01:24,793
<i>Let's stop stressing out.</i>

38
00:01:24,876 --> 00:01:25,877
<i>Right?</i>

39
00:01:26,586 --> 00:01:27,837
<i>Let me join your group.</i>

40
00:01:29,339 --> 00:01:30,632
<i>I can help.</i>

41
00:01:30,715 --> 00:01:31,966
<i>Promise.</i>

42
00:01:32,842 --> 00:01:34,761
<i>What help are you talking about?</i>

43
00:01:34,844 --> 00:01:36,137
<i>I know someone.</i>

44
00:01:36,221 --> 00:01:38,431
<i>He can give us new names</i>

45
00:01:39,474 --> 00:01:40,683
<i>and a new life.</i>

46
00:01:42,644 --> 00:01:44,646
<i>We can live as a different person</i>

47
00:01:44,729 --> 00:01:46,481
<i>without anyone going after us.</i>

48
00:01:47,232 --> 00:01:49,359
<i>Of course you need to let me in your group</i>

49
00:01:49,442 --> 00:01:51,694
<i>and help me get out of here too.</i>

50
00:01:54,239 --> 00:01:55,865
<i>Um, Billy?</i>

51
00:01:57,200 --> 00:02:01,246
<i>Some of your stuff is still in my unit.</i>

52
00:02:01,329 --> 00:02:02,831
<i>I'll just send it to you.</i>

53
00:02:03,873 --> 00:02:06,960
<i>You know you can still stay there, right?</i>

54
00:02:07,043 --> 00:02:09,087
<i>You just want to leave</i>
<i>as soon as possible.</i>

55
00:02:09,170 --> 00:02:11,256
<i>No, it's all good. Thank you, Charm.</i>

56
00:02:12,674 --> 00:02:14,884
<i>There's just too many of us.</i>

57
00:02:15,635 --> 00:02:17,679
<i>My father is staying with us now too.</i>

58
00:02:18,847 --> 00:02:19,848
<i>Thank you.</i>

59
00:02:22,851 --> 00:02:23,935
<i>You're on good terms now?</i>

60
00:02:27,814 --> 00:02:31,693
<i>He saved Oliver and Aunt Pres, so…</i>

61
00:02:33,069 --> 00:02:34,195
<i>I owe him that.</i>

62
00:02:37,282 --> 00:02:38,366
<i>Wow.</i>

63
00:02:39,159 --> 00:02:42,120
<i>It's like you're</i>
<i>a different person already.</i>

64
00:02:43,746 --> 00:02:46,374
<i>You know how to forgive now.</i>

65
00:02:49,335 --> 00:02:50,879
<i>For your brother.</i>

66
00:02:51,880 --> 00:02:53,047
<i>For Auntie Pres.</i>

67
00:02:57,969 --> 00:02:59,470
<i>And for myself.</i>

68
00:03:08,897 --> 00:03:12,317
The CCTV technician will come tomorrow.

69
00:03:12,400 --> 00:03:15,403
Yup, at 2:00 p.m.
I'll arrive at one.

70
00:03:15,486 --> 00:03:16,821
- Okay.
- Me too, boss.

71
00:03:16,905 --> 00:03:17,989
- Yes. Thank you.
- Okay.

72
00:03:18,072 --> 00:03:20,783
- Bye, boss.
- Don't forget to lock the door.

73
00:03:24,746 --> 00:03:25,705
Dude.

74
00:03:27,040 --> 00:03:28,416
I thought you went home.

75
00:03:29,125 --> 00:03:31,669
Um, I just wanted to ask something.

76
00:03:32,545 --> 00:03:33,630
What is it?

77
00:03:34,255 --> 00:03:35,673
Are we okay?

78
00:03:36,591 --> 00:03:38,301
Yeah. What do you mean?

79
00:03:39,052 --> 00:03:40,970
There's something you're not telling me.

80
00:03:41,054 --> 00:03:44,224
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

81
00:03:44,307 --> 00:03:48,478
Jordan, say it. Come on.

82
00:03:48,561 --> 00:03:49,646
What is it?

83
00:03:51,856 --> 00:03:52,941
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

84
00:03:53,524 --> 00:03:55,151
Is it that obvious?

85
00:03:58,488 --> 00:04:00,198
Jordan, please.

86
00:04:00,281 --> 00:04:05,870
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

87
00:04:05,954 --> 00:04:07,622
Right now? Um…

88
00:04:08,248 --> 00:04:09,624
Shit. Okay.

89
00:04:11,876 --> 00:04:13,086
I'll admit it.

90
00:04:14,754 --> 00:04:15,797
Dude, I…

91
00:04:17,507 --> 00:04:18,800
I'm in love with you.

92
00:04:18,883 --> 00:04:24,931
[ROMANTIC MUSIC PLAYING]

93
00:04:25,014 --> 00:04:26,057
[MUSIC STOPS]

94
00:04:27,058 --> 00:04:28,434
[BILLY] Jordan,

95
00:04:28,518 --> 00:04:29,560
say something.

96
00:04:31,396 --> 00:04:32,480
Huh?

97
00:04:33,773 --> 00:04:36,484
Is there any way we can lower the cost

98
00:04:36,567 --> 00:04:39,654
of the additional security measures
you proposed?

99
00:04:40,280 --> 00:04:41,906
Oh… that's all?

100
00:04:41,990 --> 00:04:42,991
[CHUCKLES]

101
00:04:43,074 --> 00:04:43,992
I thought…

102
00:04:45,785 --> 00:04:47,245
Thought what?

103
00:04:47,328 --> 00:04:48,663
Nothing.

104
00:04:48,746 --> 00:04:51,499
Um, okay. I'll review it again.

105
00:04:51,582 --> 00:04:52,959
Okay.

106
00:04:54,168 --> 00:04:56,379
Sorry. I'm still talking about work.

107
00:04:56,462 --> 00:04:57,422
No, it's okay.

108
00:04:58,089 --> 00:04:59,048
I understand.

109
00:04:59,549 --> 00:05:02,385
["PUZZLE" BY BELLE MARIANO PLAYING]

110
00:05:02,468 --> 00:05:05,805
If only our partnership
with Peter had gone through.

111
00:05:08,558 --> 00:05:10,560
We lost so much money, dude.

112
00:05:11,769 --> 00:05:15,356
I think Claire will push through.

113
00:05:17,275 --> 00:05:20,278
Dude, make sure you get enough rest.

114
00:05:21,654 --> 00:05:24,032
Take care of yourself, okay?

115
00:05:24,115 --> 00:05:28,870
["PUZZLE" CONTINUES]

116
00:05:28,953 --> 00:05:29,912
Good night.

117
00:05:31,789 --> 00:05:32,874
Good night.

118
00:05:45,553 --> 00:05:52,268
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

119
00:06:31,724 --> 00:06:34,018
[ROWENA] Oh, thank you
for breakfast, my dears.

120
00:06:34,102 --> 00:06:36,562
Oh, I mean brunch. [CHUCKLES]

121
00:06:36,646 --> 00:06:37,897
I'll see you then.

122
00:06:37,980 --> 00:06:39,398
[ROWENA GASPS]

123
00:06:39,482 --> 00:06:40,525
Ralph.

124
00:06:43,069 --> 00:06:46,155
Are you coming here for brunch
or to see your mom?

125
00:06:46,864 --> 00:06:49,242
Um…

126
00:06:50,201 --> 00:06:51,536
I-I just want to…

127
00:06:52,203 --> 00:06:54,122
I just need to talk to you about Charm.

128
00:06:54,205 --> 00:06:55,832
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

129
00:06:55,915 --> 00:06:57,041
[SCOFFS]

130
00:06:58,042 --> 00:07:00,711
Have you finally made up
your mind about that woman?

131
00:07:03,589 --> 00:07:05,675
Yes. Yes, Ma.

132
00:07:06,425 --> 00:07:07,301
[ROWENA] Good.

133
00:07:08,719 --> 00:07:09,804
So,

134
00:07:10,388 --> 00:07:13,558
are you here because you're
finally breaking up with her?

135
00:07:17,186 --> 00:07:18,187
No.

136
00:07:19,939 --> 00:07:22,024
She's the one breaking up with me.

137
00:07:24,569 --> 00:07:25,528
Yeah.

138
00:07:25,611 --> 00:07:32,243
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

139
00:07:32,326 --> 00:07:34,579
Do you know what she told me, Ma?

140
00:07:37,123 --> 00:07:39,083
She's willing to let me go

141
00:07:40,376 --> 00:07:42,170
just so I can make up with you.

142
00:07:43,463 --> 00:07:44,547
And Billy…

143
00:07:46,966 --> 00:07:48,301
Billy agreed with her.

144
00:07:49,510 --> 00:07:50,720
Because for her,

145
00:07:51,762 --> 00:07:53,681
it's family first.

146
00:07:56,184 --> 00:07:57,477
That's why I'm here now.

147
00:08:02,023 --> 00:08:03,065
I'm sorry, son.

148
00:08:03,149 --> 00:08:09,030
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

149
00:08:15,119 --> 00:08:17,246
[BIRDS CHIRPING]

150
00:08:17,330 --> 00:08:18,706
[GRANADO] <i>Hi, Billy.</i>

151
00:08:18,789 --> 00:08:21,042
<i>I just got off the phone</i>
<i>with Attorney Reyes,</i>

152
00:08:21,125 --> 00:08:22,460
<i>Bea's lawyer.</i>

153
00:08:23,211 --> 00:08:25,004
<i>There was an incident in the city jail.</i>

154
00:08:25,087 --> 00:08:27,048
<i>Bea's mother got into a fight.</i>

155
00:08:27,131 --> 00:08:28,299
She was provoked.

156
00:08:29,050 --> 00:08:31,552
She flipped out, hurt others,
and she got injured.

157
00:08:32,845 --> 00:08:35,264
Don't you think they just
made that up, Attorney?

158
00:08:36,724 --> 00:08:37,892
Knowing Bea…

159
00:08:38,434 --> 00:08:40,937
She's good at making up stories.

160
00:08:41,938 --> 00:08:44,273
She did that to help grant her appeal

161
00:08:44,357 --> 00:08:47,151
to transfer her mother
to a psychiatric facility.

162
00:08:47,235 --> 00:08:50,404
[SIGHS] No. It really happened.
There was medical proof.

163
00:08:50,488 --> 00:08:52,865
Attorney, I know Bea.

164
00:08:54,492 --> 00:08:57,245
If her mother gets transferred
to the hospital,

165
00:08:58,079 --> 00:08:59,705
it will be easier for them to escape.

166
00:08:59,789 --> 00:09:01,249
If that happens,

167
00:09:01,332 --> 00:09:04,085
they will be a threat to my family again.

168
00:09:04,168 --> 00:09:05,419
That's it.

169
00:09:05,503 --> 00:09:08,089
We can use that to counter Bea's appeal.

170
00:09:08,714 --> 00:09:12,552
Let them know
that no matter what she and her mom do,

171
00:09:13,177 --> 00:09:15,304
they won't be able to get out of jail.

172
00:09:15,388 --> 00:09:21,519
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

173
00:09:23,521 --> 00:09:24,981
Let me be clear.

174
00:09:25,064 --> 00:09:27,024
Bea, Attorney Reyes.

175
00:09:27,108 --> 00:09:28,859
You want to file an appeal

176
00:09:28,943 --> 00:09:31,779
to transfer Mariela
to a psychiatric facility.

177
00:09:35,491 --> 00:09:36,534
[SIGHS]

178
00:09:37,201 --> 00:09:38,703
That's what I'm hoping for, Attorney.

179
00:09:39,328 --> 00:09:41,330
My mother got hurt.

180
00:09:41,414 --> 00:09:42,582
You know,

181
00:09:42,665 --> 00:09:44,792
I wouldn't want her condition
to get worse.

182
00:09:46,335 --> 00:09:48,337
We are prepared to prove that Mariela

183
00:09:48,421 --> 00:09:51,674
should be transferred for her own safety
and the safety of others.

184
00:09:51,757 --> 00:09:53,009
Let me just remind you.

185
00:09:53,092 --> 00:09:55,595
We have strict laws when it comes to this.

186
00:09:55,678 --> 00:09:59,098
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

187
00:09:59,181 --> 00:10:00,891
What law, Attorney?

188
00:10:00,975 --> 00:10:02,435
Billy's Law.

189
00:10:03,311 --> 00:10:04,312
Bea,

190
00:10:04,812 --> 00:10:06,272
these laws are in place

191
00:10:06,355 --> 00:10:09,066
to prevent people
from faking mental illness

192
00:10:09,150 --> 00:10:10,526
to avoid punishment.

193
00:10:11,819 --> 00:10:12,778
Wait.

194
00:10:13,446 --> 00:10:15,406
Are you implying that my mom
is just faking it?

195
00:10:15,489 --> 00:10:17,450
My mom wouldn't do that.

196
00:10:17,533 --> 00:10:18,826
[SCOFFS]

197
00:10:18,909 --> 00:10:22,038
She was confined
in a psychiatric ward before.

198
00:10:22,913 --> 00:10:24,749
[GRANADO] Did she finish her treatment?

199
00:10:27,918 --> 00:10:28,919
[EXHALES DEEPLY]

200
00:10:29,003 --> 00:10:30,755
All I'm saying is,

201
00:10:31,339 --> 00:10:34,884
your appeal won't be granted easily.

202
00:10:35,468 --> 00:10:39,221
My client and I will do
everything we can to oppose this.

203
00:10:39,305 --> 00:10:42,516
We will demand a strict
competency evaluation.

204
00:10:42,600 --> 00:10:44,602
I'm sure, Attorney Reyes, you know that.

205
00:10:44,685 --> 00:10:47,104
Unless a qualified
mental health professional

206
00:10:47,188 --> 00:10:50,900
certifies that Mariela is not competent
to stand in trial,

207
00:10:50,983 --> 00:10:52,735
she has to stay in prison.

208
00:10:52,818 --> 00:10:56,697
My client is willing to undergo
any evaluation, Attorney.

209
00:10:59,158 --> 00:11:02,244
Wait, Attorney. What evaluation
are you talking about, huh?

210
00:11:02,328 --> 00:11:03,287
Isn't it obvious?

211
00:11:04,246 --> 00:11:06,374
This place isn't suitable
for my mom's condition.

212
00:11:06,457 --> 00:11:11,253
The behavior shown by Mariela isn't
synonymous with legal insanity.

213
00:11:11,337 --> 00:11:15,841
Without proof of total cognitive loss,
she can't get transferred.

214
00:11:16,717 --> 00:11:19,178
You keep spouting all this stuff.

215
00:11:19,261 --> 00:11:22,598
Synonymous, cognitive…
I don't care what it is.

216
00:11:22,681 --> 00:11:25,810
Do whatever your client wants you to do.

217
00:11:25,893 --> 00:11:27,686
But tell your client

218
00:11:27,770 --> 00:11:29,730
that I won't back down.

219
00:11:31,315 --> 00:11:34,151
I'm just clarifying your
and your mother's situation.

220
00:11:34,735 --> 00:11:36,070
So you don't waste your time.

221
00:11:36,153 --> 00:11:38,948
Oh, I'm not wasting anything!
I have plenty of time here.

222
00:11:39,031 --> 00:11:42,910
I'll keep myself busy
fighting for my mother's rights.

223
00:11:43,577 --> 00:11:46,288
Sure, that's your right.

224
00:11:46,372 --> 00:11:48,124
But let me remind you

225
00:11:48,207 --> 00:11:50,626
that my client is living a quiet life now.

226
00:11:50,709 --> 00:11:55,089
And she, we, are determined
to keep it that way.

227
00:11:57,883 --> 00:12:00,928
What did you say?
Your client is living a quiet life now?

228
00:12:01,011 --> 00:12:02,430
Why? Is she happy?

229
00:12:02,513 --> 00:12:04,348
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

230
00:12:04,432 --> 00:12:06,267
[BEA SCOFFS] Is she happy now?

231
00:12:06,767 --> 00:12:08,811
Because her father is with them now?

232
00:12:08,894 --> 00:12:11,147
They're like one
big happy family. Is that it?

233
00:12:11,230 --> 00:12:12,523
[SCOFFS]

234
00:12:12,606 --> 00:12:13,607
That's perfect.

235
00:12:13,691 --> 00:12:15,943
Give your client my congratulations!

236
00:12:16,026 --> 00:12:17,486
I hope they're having a blast!

237
00:12:17,570 --> 00:12:19,947
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

238
00:12:20,030 --> 00:12:21,782
What's the real reason, Bea?

239
00:12:22,533 --> 00:12:25,494
Why do you want to ruin my client's life?

240
00:12:34,753 --> 00:12:36,255
I'm done here, Attorney.

241
00:12:45,264 --> 00:12:46,682
For the US market,

242
00:12:46,765 --> 00:12:49,852
we need a completely different
positioning strategy.

243
00:12:49,935 --> 00:12:53,606
I want the brand messaging
to reflect momentum.

244
00:12:53,689 --> 00:12:56,692
Something modern, emotionally direct,

245
00:12:56,775 --> 00:12:58,903
but still premium.

246
00:12:58,986 --> 00:13:03,032
That's why we are moving forward
with our new tagline,

247
00:13:03,115 --> 00:13:05,242
"Real Love In Real Time."

248
00:13:05,326 --> 00:13:06,785
- Oh.
- [CLAPPING]

249
00:13:06,869 --> 00:13:07,995
[BLAIRE] Nice.

250
00:13:09,747 --> 00:13:11,040
It communicates

251
00:13:11,123 --> 00:13:13,334
urgency but not recklessness.

252
00:13:13,417 --> 00:13:14,835
So the idea is,

253
00:13:14,919 --> 00:13:16,545
meaningful connections,

254
00:13:16,629 --> 00:13:18,297
intelligently matched,

255
00:13:18,380 --> 00:13:19,715
delivered at the pace

256
00:13:19,798 --> 00:13:21,592
people actually live today.

257
00:13:21,675 --> 00:13:24,762
[CLAPPING]

258
00:13:24,845 --> 00:13:28,015
So once everything is approved,
we will release it

259
00:13:28,098 --> 00:13:30,267
on all of our social media platforms,

260
00:13:30,351 --> 00:13:31,936
which are currently being prepared

261
00:13:32,019 --> 00:13:35,481
by Val and Marj as we speak.

262
00:13:36,315 --> 00:13:37,399
You can clap now.

263
00:13:37,483 --> 00:13:41,028
- [CLAPPING]
- [TONI CHUCKLES]

264
00:13:41,111 --> 00:13:42,488
Ralph.

265
00:13:42,571 --> 00:13:44,156
You may want to add something?

266
00:13:45,241 --> 00:13:46,242
- Uh…
- Uh…

267
00:13:46,867 --> 00:13:49,662
Chief, looks like you're hiding
something from us.

268
00:13:49,745 --> 00:13:52,540
Is Ralph going to invest in it too?

269
00:13:52,623 --> 00:13:53,749
[CHARM] Hmm?

270
00:13:53,832 --> 00:13:56,961
Well, I agree with
Billy's take on the US market

271
00:13:57,044 --> 00:13:58,462
and how we will approach it.

272
00:13:58,546 --> 00:14:01,173
The idea that life doesn't slow down.

273
00:14:01,257 --> 00:14:02,758
Because if

274
00:14:02,841 --> 00:14:04,802
you've set your mind on something…

275
00:14:05,386 --> 00:14:06,554
[SIGHS, CLICKS TONGUE]

276
00:14:06,637 --> 00:14:08,180
…you don't wait for the perfect time.

277
00:14:09,473 --> 00:14:10,975
You choose the moment.

278
00:14:14,311 --> 00:14:15,604
Because

279
00:14:17,106 --> 00:14:18,399
real love…

280
00:14:19,066 --> 00:14:20,693
Real love isn't just a feeling.

281
00:14:23,404 --> 00:14:28,993
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

282
00:14:31,370 --> 00:14:33,330
It's a decision you make.

283
00:14:33,914 --> 00:14:34,999
Right here.

284
00:14:35,958 --> 00:14:37,251
Right now.

285
00:14:40,546 --> 00:14:42,756
[EXHALES DEEPLY]
Okay. Um…

286
00:14:43,716 --> 00:14:46,051
What I'm trying to say is

287
00:14:46,135 --> 00:14:47,303
that even if

288
00:14:49,096 --> 00:14:51,849
a lot of people are against us,

289
00:14:53,058 --> 00:14:54,101
Charm…

290
00:14:57,897 --> 00:14:59,023
will you marry me?

291
00:15:01,483 --> 00:15:06,906
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

292
00:15:06,989 --> 00:15:08,157
Um…

293
00:15:09,909 --> 00:15:11,452
Ralph, let's talk first.

294
00:15:12,578 --> 00:15:13,662
What?

295
00:15:14,371 --> 00:15:15,539
Babe.

296
00:15:15,623 --> 00:15:17,207
Didn't I tell you

297
00:15:17,291 --> 00:15:20,169
to fix your relationship
with your mom first?

298
00:15:21,045 --> 00:15:23,047
Babe, that's more important.

299
00:15:24,214 --> 00:15:26,717
But I want to say yes,
knowing that she will be happy

300
00:15:26,800 --> 00:15:27,968
with our decision.

301
00:15:31,805 --> 00:15:34,600
I'll be the happiest
if you will say yes, dear.

302
00:15:37,436 --> 00:15:39,063
My son said that

303
00:15:39,688 --> 00:15:43,859
you're willing to let him go just
so that he can fix our relationship.

304
00:15:44,735 --> 00:15:45,736
And Billy,

305
00:15:45,819 --> 00:15:48,572
you never stopped telling my son
to always reach out to me.

306
00:15:49,281 --> 00:15:50,240
Thank you

307
00:15:50,866 --> 00:15:53,869
to you and Charm

308
00:15:54,578 --> 00:15:57,289
for making me realize
that I've been wrong

309
00:15:57,873 --> 00:15:59,249
and selfish.

310
00:15:59,833 --> 00:16:01,877
Charm, I'm so sorry.

311
00:16:05,005 --> 00:16:06,340
Daughter. [CHUCKLES]

312
00:16:08,050 --> 00:16:11,387
Ralph, what are you waiting for?
Ask her again.

313
00:16:11,470 --> 00:16:12,304
Okay.

314
00:16:12,388 --> 00:16:13,555
- Uh…
- [CLAPPING]

315
00:16:13,639 --> 00:16:14,974
Take… Take two?

316
00:16:15,057 --> 00:16:16,141
- Take two. Okay.
- Take two.

317
00:16:16,225 --> 00:16:17,559
- [ROWENA] You can do it.
- All right.

318
00:16:17,643 --> 00:16:19,687
[ROWENA] Okay. Kneel. Do it properly.

319
00:16:20,646 --> 00:16:22,731
- Uh, Charm.
- Mm?

320
00:16:23,273 --> 00:16:24,149
[RALPH] Babe?

321
00:16:25,109 --> 00:16:26,694
W-Will you marry me?

322
00:16:27,945 --> 00:16:29,113
- Yes!
- [RALPH CHUCKLES]

323
00:16:29,196 --> 00:16:30,823
Of course, yes!

324
00:16:31,448 --> 00:16:32,408
Oh my God.

325
00:16:32,950 --> 00:16:34,159
[ROWENA] Wow.

326
00:16:36,161 --> 00:16:38,455
- [ROWENA] Son…
- Thank you, Ma.

327
00:16:39,164 --> 00:16:41,667
- Thank you, Ma.
- Oh my gosh!

328
00:16:41,750 --> 00:16:44,628
- Happy family!
- Thank you!

329
00:16:44,712 --> 00:16:46,255
- Thank you, guys.
- Congrats.

330
00:16:46,338 --> 00:16:48,966
- Hi, Auntie.
- Thank you!

331
00:16:57,683 --> 00:17:00,978
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

332
00:17:01,061 --> 00:17:04,898
[KEYBOARD KEYS CLACKING]

333
00:17:14,408 --> 00:17:16,952
THE COUNTRY'S NEWS

334
00:17:20,497 --> 00:17:26,253
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

335
00:17:26,336 --> 00:17:29,465
A HOUSE BURNED DOWN
ON SAN ISIDRO STREET

336
00:17:29,548 --> 00:17:32,801
MOTHER LEFT INJURED
AND DAUGHTER DEAD

337
00:17:39,558 --> 00:17:42,561
[KEYBOARD KEYS CLACKING]

338
00:17:43,896 --> 00:17:45,898
- Eric?
- Hi, ma'am.

339
00:17:46,648 --> 00:17:50,444
How's the search for your other family?

340
00:17:50,527 --> 00:17:54,156
The article's publisher
still hasn't wrote back to me.

341
00:17:54,239 --> 00:17:56,241
I've also contacted the reporter

342
00:17:56,325 --> 00:17:59,620
who wrote about the fire,
but I've got nothing.

343
00:17:59,703 --> 00:18:01,413
I'm trying to follow up on them.

344
00:18:01,497 --> 00:18:03,457
I've sent an email to another journalist.

345
00:18:04,208 --> 00:18:05,375
But no one's answered.

346
00:18:05,459 --> 00:18:07,377
They were caught in a fire too?

347
00:18:07,461 --> 00:18:10,798
My eldest daughter died in that incident.

348
00:18:10,881 --> 00:18:12,549
I go to her grave once in a while,

349
00:18:12,633 --> 00:18:16,970
hoping that her mom
and sister would visit,

350
00:18:17,054 --> 00:18:18,680
but…

351
00:18:19,681 --> 00:18:21,934
And you found Billy's family first.

352
00:18:24,853 --> 00:18:26,730
Does Billy know

353
00:18:26,814 --> 00:18:29,274
that she has siblings other than Oliver?

354
00:18:29,358 --> 00:18:31,985
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

355
00:18:32,069 --> 00:18:34,738
I don't know how to tell her.

356
00:18:34,822 --> 00:18:36,281
I don't want to hurt her.

357
00:18:36,865 --> 00:18:38,534
I'm sure she'll get mad again.

358
00:18:39,952 --> 00:18:41,161
Oh, Eric.

359
00:18:41,245 --> 00:18:43,831
Aren't you tired of living a lie?

360
00:18:43,914 --> 00:18:46,083
If I were you, I'd tell her everything.

361
00:18:46,166 --> 00:18:47,751
Sure, she's going to get hurt,

362
00:18:47,835 --> 00:18:50,796
but that's better than
lying to her forever.

363
00:18:52,965 --> 00:18:56,135
[MUSIC BUILDS, FADES]

364
00:18:56,218 --> 00:18:57,928
Pa, there's a fight back there.

365
00:18:58,011 --> 00:18:59,805
- Let's go watch.
- I'll get going.

366
00:18:59,888 --> 00:19:00,931
- Bye.
- Bye, Ms. Lucy.

367
00:19:01,014 --> 00:19:02,182
- All right.
- Let's go.

368
00:19:02,266 --> 00:19:04,268
- Wait.
- Hurry!

369
00:19:04,810 --> 00:19:06,019
Where are you going to take me?

370
00:19:06,103 --> 00:19:08,105
Right out back. Let's go!

371
00:19:08,772 --> 00:19:10,899
[OLIVER] There's a fight going on!

372
00:19:10,983 --> 00:19:12,609
- [ENRICO] What is it?
- [OLIVER] Over there!

373
00:19:12,693 --> 00:19:13,819
- Where--
- There's a fight!

374
00:19:13,902 --> 00:19:15,237
- Auntie…
- [ENRICO] Wait up!

375
00:19:15,320 --> 00:19:16,989
- Hurry up!
- Calm down.

376
00:19:17,072 --> 00:19:18,240
Hurry!

377
00:19:18,323 --> 00:19:19,158
Why--

378
00:19:20,659 --> 00:19:22,870
- [SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]
- [ENRICO EXHALES]

379
00:19:22,953 --> 00:19:24,121
- Ta-da!
- [BILLY CLEARS THROAT]

380
00:19:24,705 --> 00:19:26,623
Did you think we forgot?

381
00:19:26,707 --> 00:19:28,083
[OLIVER CLAPPING]

382
00:19:28,167 --> 00:19:29,918
Happy birthday.

383
00:19:33,922 --> 00:19:35,215
Happy birthday, Dad.

384
00:19:35,299 --> 00:19:37,342
[OLIVER] Make a wish! Make a wish!

385
00:19:38,135 --> 00:19:39,094
Boom!

386
00:19:41,263 --> 00:19:42,389
[CHUCKLES]

387
00:19:42,472 --> 00:19:43,640
Thank you.

388
00:19:45,767 --> 00:19:48,604
I'll take you
to Billy's favorite restaurant.

389
00:19:48,687 --> 00:19:50,272
They serve seafood there.

390
00:19:50,355 --> 00:19:51,732
Do you like seafood?

391
00:19:52,399 --> 00:19:53,817
<i>♪ Happy birthday to you ♪</i>

392
00:19:53,901 --> 00:19:55,861
- Okay. Let's go, Auntie Pres?
- [PRECIOUS] Mm.

393
00:19:55,944 --> 00:19:58,822
- Okay, let's bring this.
- Let's box it up.

394
00:19:58,906 --> 00:20:05,329
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

395
00:20:05,412 --> 00:20:06,705
[DRAMATIC STING]

396
00:20:14,004 --> 00:20:15,923
<i>Is everything ready</i>
<i>for Family Day?</i>

397
00:20:16,006 --> 00:20:17,799
[INMATE] <i>We checked last night.</i>
<i>They replaced the railings.</i>

398
00:20:17,883 --> 00:20:19,218
<i>You and your father are okay now?</i>

399
00:20:19,301 --> 00:20:20,928
<i>Has he gotten his act together?</i>

400
00:20:21,011 --> 00:20:23,555
<i>Happy and all together.</i>

401
00:20:23,639 --> 00:20:25,599
[OLIVER] <i>Of course, Papa.</i>

402
00:20:25,682 --> 00:20:27,226
<i>We won't be apart anymore.</i>

403
00:20:27,309 --> 00:20:30,729
<i>I want to leave.</i>
<i>I can't take it anymore.</i>

404
00:20:30,812 --> 00:20:33,023
<i>I just want you to reassure me</i>

405
00:20:33,106 --> 00:20:36,360
<i>that Bea can't do anything else</i>
<i>to help herself and her mother.</i>

406
00:20:36,443 --> 00:20:39,404
<i>Mariela still needs to undergo</i>
<i>psychiatric evaluation.</i>

407
00:20:39,488 --> 00:20:41,657
<i>So Bea still has a chance of</i>
<i>getting what she wants?</i>

408
00:20:43,242 --> 00:20:45,994
<i>What happened to us</i>
<i>was devastating.</i>

409
00:20:46,078 --> 00:20:50,249
<i>But when I found out</i>
<i>that Dad didn't forget about me,</i>

410
00:20:50,332 --> 00:20:52,751
<i>everything we had lost</i>
<i>didn't seem to matter anymore.</i>

411
00:20:52,834 --> 00:20:55,212
<i>Because Dad came back to us.</i>

412
00:20:55,295 --> 00:20:57,130
[BEA] <i>The truth won't hurt us.</i>

413
00:20:57,214 --> 00:20:59,800
<i>It may even save us both.</i>

414
00:20:59,883 --> 00:21:02,427
<i>I can request to speak to Billy, right?</i>

415
00:21:02,511 --> 00:21:03,470
<i>I'm your lawyer.</i>

416
00:21:03,553 --> 00:21:07,182
<i>Anything you intend to say to her</i>
<i>should go through me first.</i>

417
00:21:07,266 --> 00:21:10,978
<i>I want to talk to her alone</i>
<i>and tell her myself.</i>
